HARMONY-VOICE — Theoretical Foundations for Expressive Singing Voice Synthesis on a Robot

Ouadi Maakoul and SI TEAM


Document: Founding Thesis, final theoretical version (v1.0-theory)


Epistemological Preamble

Three registers are used without exception:

· [E] — Established. A result, method, or convention from the published literature. SI TEAM claims no ownership. The citation is described in prose because this volume carries no bibliography; the reader is expected to locate the primary source from the description.
· [C] — Conjecture. A theoretical proposition of Ouadi Maakoul and SI TEAM. Argued, formalised, and falsifiable, but not validated.
· [TD] — To Demonstrate. A planned empirical chapter whose outcome may refute the corresponding conjecture.

A theoretical thesis that does not state the conditions of its own refutation is not a thesis. It is a position statement. This volume is therefore constructed so that its central claim can be attacked at named points with named procedures. The absence of empirical results is not a weakness to be concealed; it is the condition under which the theoretical content can be judged on its own merits, before data can be used to rationalise it.

