2. Formal Framework

2.1 Control Space

Let T>0 be the duration of a sung item. The control space is the product

\mathcal{U} \;=\; \mathcal{S}\times \mathcal{C}\big([0,T];\mathbb{R}^4\big)\times \mathcal{D},

where:

· \mathcal{S}\subset\mathbb{R}^d is the global style space — a vector, not a trajectory, encoding timbre, vocal technique, and perceived vocal effort. Its role is to condition the frame-level dynamics.
· \mathcal{C}([0,T];\mathbb{R}^4) is the space of continuous four-component trajectories \mathbf{c}(t)=\big(F_0(t),E(t),B(t),V(t)\big), with F_0 in cents relative to a reference, E in dB relative to peak, B\in[0,1] a breathiness index, and V encoding vibrato rate and depth jointly.
· \mathcal{D}=\{(p_k,t_k^{\mathrm{on}},t_k^{\mathrm{off}})\} is the discrete sequence of phonemes with onset and offset times.

An element is written u=(s,\mathbf{c},D).

Notational correction [E]. The symbol \mathcal{C}^4 is avoided throughout: in analysis it conventionally denotes four-times continuous differentiability, which is not intended here. The space is written \mathcal{C}([0,T];\mathbb{R}^4) — continuous functions into \mathbb{R}^4 — and no differentiability is assumed.

Voicing mask [C]. Fundamental frequency is undefined on unvoiced segments. We therefore carry a voicing indicator v:[0,T]\to\{0,1\} and require that all F_0-dependent quantities — the trajectory, its derivative bound, and every metric of §4 that references F_0 — be evaluated on the voiced support \mathcal{T}_v=\{t: v(t)=1\} only. Metrics that ignore the mask will report artefacts on fricatives and silences; this is stated as a design requirement, not as a discovery.

2.2 Admissible Region with Joint Constraints

The admissible set is defined by a single joint feasibility map, not by independent bounds:

\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{adm}} \;=\; \big\{\, u\in\mathcal{U} \;:\; \Psi(s,\mathbf{c},D)\le 0 \,\big\},

with the following three families of constraints inside \Psi.

(i) Physiological bounds. F_0\in[F_{\min},F_{\max}] on \mathcal{T}_v; E\in[E_{\min},E_{\max}]; B\in[0,1]. The numerical values of F_{\min},F_{\max},E_{\min},E_{\max} are declared conventions for the campaign and are labelled as such; they are not derived from a source.

(ii) Derivative bounds. |\dot F_0(t)|\le v_{\max} on \mathcal{T}_v. The value of v_{\max} must be derived from corpus quantiles of the reference material and is explicitly not borrowed from speech-velocity norms: portamento, glissando, and tahrir-type melisma legitimately exceed speech-like pitch velocities, and a speech-derived bound would forbid exactly the ornamentation the thesis intends to control.

(iii) Coupling constraints [C]. Empirical relations between style and dynamics. Schematically, a breathy style implies a breathiness floor and an energy ceiling; a falsetto style implies a restricted pitch range. Two warnings are attached, and they are part of the thesis rather than footnotes to it:

· Every example inequality in this subsection is a placeholder. It becomes binding only after a posterior-predictive check on a reference corpus of labelled professional singing. Until that check passes, no inequality may be used to exclude a candidate u, because an unvalidated constraint would silently define the answer.
· At least one plausible inequality is stylistically false. The common assumption that falsetto implies reduced vibrato depth does not hold in general; falsetto with vibrato is ordinary. An inequality of this form must be tested before use, and if it fails the posterior-predictive check, it is deleted rather than weakened.

Coupling functional [C]. To make (T) measurable rather than rhetorical, we define a coupling functional on the dynamic component,

\kappa(\mathbf{c}) \;=\; \mathbb{I}\big(F_0;\,(E,B)\;\big|\;D\big),

the conditional mutual information between pitch and the pair (energy, breathiness) given the phoneme sequence, estimated on the voiced support. A copula parameter \theta across the same triple is an admissible alternative estimator when the marginals are non-Gaussian; the two are reported together and their disagreement is itself diagnostic. \kappa plays two roles: it defines the dose in a dose–response design (§6.2) and it supplies the quantity that the margin-matched baseline must be shown to reduce to zero.

2.3 Synthesis Operator and Determinism

Let \mathcal{V}:\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{adm}}\to L^2([0,T]) be the synthesis operator.

Requirement 1 (functional determinism, conditional on the seed) [C]. For fixed u and fixed seed \sigma, the distribution of \mathcal{V}(u;\sigma) is degenerate. The earlier formulation — "the distribution is degenerate" without qualification — is withdrawn, because it contradicted the existence of seeded stochastic micro-variation. Determinism is a property of the pair (u,\sigma), not of u alone.

Seeding. Stochastic micro-variation is seeded from content only:

\sigma \;=\; \mathrm{hash}\big(\text{lyrics}\,\|\,\text{melody}\,\|\,\text{style\_id}\big).

Correction [C]. The execution environment is not included in the seed. Including it would make the output differ across machines by design, which is the opposite of what a reproducibility contract should achieve. The environment is logged and published separately as a declared artefact, so that a change of environment is visible as a change of experiment rather than silently absorbed into the stochastic stream.

Requirement 2 (numerical insensitivity, primary) [C]. The scientifically relevant robustness claim is not bit-exactness. It is that the preference distribution is invariant under permitted numerical variation: different valid kernel algorithm selections, tensor-float mode enabled versus disabled, and different but equally valid reduction orders. The probe is a distributional-equivalence test on the preference outcome under these variations.

Requirement 3 (bit-exact release artefact, secondary) [C]. For the released stimulus set, bit-exactness is required and tested, but it is demoted from a theoretical claim to an engineering release contract. Its failure on new hardware refutes the engineering contract; it does not refute the theory, because listeners hear frozen rendered files.

Engineering conditions that must be stated explicitly [E]. On current GPU stacks, bit-exactness silently fails unless tensor-float matrix multiplication is disabled, the cuBLAS workspace configuration is fixed, deterministic algorithm flags are enabled, and reduction order is serialised where non-associativity would otherwise produce run-to-run variation. These are named here because omitting them produces a contract that looks rigorous and is not.

2.4 Perceptual Space

Let \mathcal{P} be an abstract perceptual space with preference relation \succ. Naturalness is a latent construct N:L^2([0,T])\to\mathbb{R} — not an acoustic property, not directly computable, and not assumed to be unidimensional until the diagnostics of §3.3 say otherwise.

