Appendix B — Formal Definitions and Derivations

B.1 Admissible Region, Written Out

The admissible region is the zero-sublevel set of a single scalar map:

\Psi(s,\mathbf{c},D)=\max\Big\{\Psi_{\mathrm{phys}},\ \Psi_{\mathrm{deriv}},\ \Psi_{\mathrm{couple}}\Big\}\le 0 .

Each block is a maximum over individual inequalities, so that \Psi\le 0 is equivalent to the conjunction of all constraints:

\Psi_{\mathrm{phys}}=\max\Big\{\tfrac{F_{\min}-F_0(t)}{1\ \mathrm{cent}},\ \tfrac{F_0(t)-F_{\max}}{1\ \mathrm{cent}},\ \tfrac{E_{\min}-E(t)}{1\ \mathrm{dB}},\ \tfrac{E(t)-E_{\max}}{1\ \mathrm{dB}},\ -B(t),\ B(t)-1\Big\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}_v},

\Psi_{\mathrm{deriv}}=\max_{t\in\mathcal{T}_v}\Big\{\tfrac{|\dot F_0(t)|-v_{\max}}{1\ \mathrm{cent/s}}\Big\},

\Psi_{\mathrm{couple}}=\max_{j}\Big\{g_j(s,\mathbf{c},D)\Big\},

where the g_j are the coupling inequalities of §2.2. The normalisation denominators are dimensional bookkeeping, not tunable parameters; they fix the units in which the max is taken.

Design parameters, declared as conventions [C]:

· E_{\min}=-60 dB, E_{\max}=0 dB: declared conventions, not sourced.
· v_{\max}: must be derived from corpus quantiles of the reference material (see B.4). It is not set a priori and is not inherited from speech-velocity norms.
· F_{\min},F_{\max}: item-specific, taken from the score's ambitus plus a declared margin.

B.2 The Coupling Functional

Definition.

\kappa(\mathbf{c})=\mathbb{I}\big(F_0;\,(E,B)\mid D\big),

the conditional mutual information between the pitch trajectory and the pair (energy, breathiness), conditioned on the phoneme sequence, evaluated on \mathcal{T}_v.

Why conditioned on D. Phoneme identity induces dependence between pitch and energy for purely linguistic reasons (stress, vowel openness). Conditioning on D removes this induced component and leaves the prosodic-musical coupling, which is the quantity the thesis claims is causal.

Plug-in estimator with bias correction [E]. Discretise (F_0,E,B) into K bins per dimension on \mathcal{T}_v, form the empirical joint counts n_{ijk\ell}, and estimate

\hat{\mathbb{I}}=\sum_{i,j,k,\ell}\frac{n_{ijk\ell}}{n}\log\frac{n_{ijk\ell}\,n_{k\ell}}{n_{ik\ell}\,n_{jk\ell}},

then correct the finite-sample bias by the Miller–Madow term

\hat{\mathbb{I}}_{\mathrm{MM}}=\hat{\mathbb{I}}+\frac{|\mathcal{B}|-1}{2n\ln 2},

with |\mathcal{B}| the number of occupied cells. The bin count K is selected by a stability criterion: K is increased until \hat{\mathbb{I}}_{\mathrm{MM}} changes by less than a declared fraction across two successive doublings. The chosen K is reported.

Alternative estimator. A copula-based dependence parameter \theta (Gaussian copula correlation, or a vine-copula parameter for three variables) is estimated on the same support. The two are reported together; their disagreement is diagnostic and is reported rather than resolved.

Fallback estimator. When |\mathcal{T}_v| is small (short items), a k-nearest-neighbour conditional mutual information estimator is substituted, with the neighbour count fixed in advance. The fallback is declared before the campaign so that it cannot be chosen post hoc to produce a convenient number.

B.3 Dose–Response Variable

Let \lambda\in[0,\lambda_{\max}] be a coupling-strength dial. Trajectories are generated by interpolating between the independence copula (\lambda=0) and the corpus-estimated copula (\lambda=1), with the marginals held fixed at the proposed system's own marginals. \lambda>1 corresponds to extrapolation beyond the corpus-implied dependence, and is included deliberately to test for an interior optimum. The ladder is pre-registered; the number of levels is fixed before generation.

B.4 Derivation of v_{\max} from Corpus Quantiles

For a reference corpus of labelled professional singing with aligned pitch tracks:

1. Compute |\dot F_0(t)| on \mathcal{T}_v for all items.
2. Stratify by segment type: sustained, transition, portamento/glissando, ornament.
3. Set v_{\max} to a high quantile (declared before inspection) of the ornament stratum, not the sustained stratum.

Rationale [C]. A bound taken from sustained segments would forbid glissando and tahrir. A bound taken from the ornament stratum permits them while still excluding non-musical slides. The stratum choice is stated in advance because it is a substantive modelling decision, not a numerical detail.

B.5 Posterior-Predictive Check for Coupling Inequalities

Each candidate inequality g_j\le 0 is tested as follows.

1. Fit a hierarchical generative model of (s,\mathbf{c},D) on the reference corpus.
2. Draw M replicate datasets from the posterior predictive distribution.
3. For each replicate, compute the proportion of observations violating g_j.
4. Declare g_j binding only if this proportion is below a declared small value (e.g., 0.05) in at least a declared majority of replicates.

Until a g_j passes, it is a placeholder and cannot exclude a candidate u. This rule exists because an unvalidated constraint silently defines the answer.

