Appendix G — Comparator Construction

G.1 Baseline 1 — Mechanical

Sustained pitches at the scored durations, constant energy, zero breathiness, no vibrato, no micro-variation. Purpose: lower bound and calibration stimulus. Explicitly insufficient alone.

G.2 Baseline 2 — Margin-Matched, Structure-Destroyed

Construction A: copula.

1. Estimate the marginal laws \hat F_{F_0},\hat F_E,\hat F_B from the proposed system's own output on the item.
2. Transform each trajectory to uniform scale: u_j(t)=\hat F_j(x_j(t)).
3. Reassign the dependence structure: replace the empirical copula by the independence copula (for the strong form) or by a fitted parametric copula with a declared parameter (for the graded form).
4. Transform back: x_j^{\mathrm{base}}(t)=\hat F_j^{-1}(u_j'(t)).

The result has the same marginals by construction and a destroyed joint structure.

Construction B: IAAFT surrogates.

1. Take the observed trajectory and compute its amplitude spectrum.
2. Iterate: (i) impose the observed amplitude spectrum on the current surrogate by Fourier transform, randomising phases; (ii) rank-map the result back onto the observed amplitude distribution.
3. Iterate until the marginal distribution and the spectrum both match within declared tolerances.

The result preserves the power spectrum and the marginal amplitude distribution while destroying nonlinear temporal dependence.

Mandatory pre-registration. Before generation, declare:

· the marginal-equivalence test family (Kolmogorov–Smirnov and Anderson–Darling per component),
· the acceptance criterion per test,
· the number of tests and the multiplicity correction,
· the generator seed,
· the \kappa reduction criterion: the baseline must show \kappa indistinguishable from zero (or from the fitted independence value) under the same estimator used for the proposed system.

A baseline that fails marginal equivalence is not a test of (T). It is a second mechanical baseline and must be reported as such.

G.3 Baseline 3 — Technique-Aware but Weakly Coupled

Technique labels are applied to condition the synthesis, but the joint constraints \Psi_{\mathrm{couple}} are not enforced. This baseline isolates any technique conditioning from specific joint conditioning.

G.4 Mandatory Strong Open Comparator

An open, technique-controllable singing synthesis system is included as a required comparator. Integration requirements: identical lyrics and melody, identical sample rate, identical loudness calibration, and identical playback chain. The system version and configuration are recorded in the environment manifest. Its performance characteristics are reported as observed, not as assumed.

G.5 Dose–Response Ladder

Coupling strength \lambda is set to a pre-registered ladder including 0, intermediate levels, 1 (corpus-implied), and at least one over-coupled level. For each level the same marginals are preserved. The preference curve across levels is estimated and tested for monotonicity or interior optimum, as declared in advance.

