Appendix J — Statistical Analysis Specification

J.1 Primary Model

Let y_{i j k} be the preference outcome for listener i, item j, condition k. The Bradley–Terry mixed-effects model is

\mathrm{logit}\big[P(y_{i j k}=1)\big]=\beta_k+u_i+v_j+w_{k i}+z_{k j},

with u_i\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\tau_u^2) a listener random intercept, v_j\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\tau_v^2) an item random intercept, w_{k i} a condition slope varying by listener, and z_{k j} a condition slope varying by item only if the item count makes the slope defensible; otherwise z_{k j} is replaced by a fixed condition-by-item interaction and the conclusion is scoped accordingly.

J.2 Effect of Interest

The quantity p is the marginal preference proportion for the proposed system over the named comparator, obtained by averaging the model's fitted probabilities over the observed listener and item distribution (a marginal, not a conditional, estimand). The choice of marginal estimand is declared in advance because conditional and marginal estimands differ under a non-linear link.

J.3 Interval Estimation

Listener-stratified bootstrap with replacement at the listener level, a declared number of resamples, and percentile intervals reported alongside bias-corrected intervals. The bootstrap unit is the listener, because clustering is at the listener level.

J.4 Three-Outcome Rule, Formally

Let [L,U] be the interval for p and let \delta be the SESOI.

· Conclusive win: L>0.5+\delta.
· Equivalence to comparator: U<0.5+\delta, established by a two-one-sided-tests procedure against the equivalence bound.
· Inconclusive: L\le 0.5+\delta\le U.

No claim of refutation is licensed in the third case.

J.5 Multiplicity

The three confirmatory contrasts form a pre-registered family. Family-wise error is controlled by a step-down procedure applied to the family. Exploratory analyses are labelled exploratory and do not support (T).

J.6 Missing and Excluded Data

Exclusion rules are declared before data collection: failed attention checks, failed consistency screen, incomplete sessions, and technical faults. The exclusion rate per rule is reported. Sensitivity analyses with and without exclusions are reported. No exclusion is introduced after inspecting the direction of the effect.

J.7 Sensitivity Analyses

Declared in advance: (i) analysis without the consistency screen; (ii) analysis treating "no preference" as a third outcome in a multinomial model; (iii) analysis with item as a fixed effect; (iv) analysis restricted to the first trial per condition per listener; (v) analysis under an alternative link function.

J.8 Reporting

All hypotheses tested, all estimates with intervals, all p-values including non-significant ones, the exclusion counts, the consistency rates, the loudness calibration record, the environment manifest hash, and the stimulus hash manifest.

