Appendix P — Glossary

Admissible region. The set of control configurations satisfying physiological, derivative, and coupling constraints.

Bit-exact release contract. A promise that a frozen stimulus set hashes identically when re-rendered on a declared environment.

Circular triad. A triple of items on which preferences cycle.

Coupling functional. The conditional mutual information between pitch and the pair (energy, breathiness) given the phoneme sequence; the quantity the thesis names as causal.

Dose–response ladder. A graded set of coupling strengths used to estimate the shape of the preference curve.

Functional determinism. The condition that a fixed input and seed yield a degenerate output distribution.

Margin-matched baseline. A structure-destroyed comparator whose per-component marginal statistics match the proposed system's, so that the only difference is joint dependence.

Numerical insensitivity. Invariance of the preference distribution under permitted numerical variation.

SESOI. Smallest effect size of interest; the bound used in the three-outcome rule.

Surrogate. An automatic predictor used only for search, never for inference, and only above a declared correlation floor.

